a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/superpowers/writing-plans/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>writing-skills</name>\n    <description>Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/superpowers/writing-skills/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>trycycle</name>\n    <description>Invoke trycycle only when the user requests it by name.</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/trycycle/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>typeset</name>\n    <description>Improves typography by fixing font choices, hierarchy, sizing, weight, and readability so text feels intentional. Use when the user mentions fonts, type, readability, text hierarchy, sizing looks off, or wants more polished, intentional typography.</description>\n    <location>/Users/nick/.agents/skills/typeset/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>\n</skills>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/Users/nick/code/roast.faster-tests-05-control-doctor-timeouts\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1795668095579,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"live_context_annotate","description":"Create, resolve, or list branch-local continuity annotations. Create uses a current mirror block ID or active Pi entry ID. pin keeps a bounded exact textual source visible; continuity keeps a durable reason/next-action pointer; archive is recall-only.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["action"],"properties":{"action":{"type":"string","enum":["create","resolve","list"]},"source":{"type":"string","description":"Current CTX_TURN block ID or active-branch Pi entry ID"},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Annotation ID for resolve"},"title":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":120},"reason":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":400},"futureAction":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":400},"retention":{"type":"string","enum":["pin","continuity","archive"]},"resolution":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":400}}}},{"name":"live_context_recall","description":"Recall the exact textual source for a branch-local annotation by ID. Output is bounded to 128-8000 estimated tokens (default 2000) and validated against the durable Pi entry's content hash.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["id"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Durable live-context annotation ID"},"maxTokens":{"type":"integer","minimum":128,"maximum":8000}}}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<file name=\"/var/folders/wc/j7p9ktnx3d99v5xm95s9h2480000gn/T/redeye-1795668094583-vpw9snh0fhr.md\">\n---- SPEC CONTEXT ----\n# Make the test suite substantially faster\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nDevelopers wait too long for feedback from the test suite. A measured\nlocal run took 143.6 seconds for 974 test cases and 7,694 assertions.\nThe suite runs cases serially, exercises many real Git repositories and\nsubprocesses, and waits for production timeouts and retry backoff. Much\nof that coverage is useful, but elapsed time is not itself evidence of\ncorrect behavior.\n\nThe full suite needs to remain a trustworthy release and CI gate while\ndevelopers get substantially faster feedback. Fast focused checks should\nalso remain available during development.\n\n## Solution\n\nRun independent test groups concurrently in isolated processes, and\nreplace unnecessary real-time waits with controllable test dependencies.\nPreserve behavioral coverage, including representative real Git, gate,\nHTTP, timeout, cancellation, and subprocess integration tests.\n\nKeep the existing full-suite command and CI gate reliable. Measure the\nresult against the current serial baseline on the same machine. Aim for\nat least a 50% reduction in full-suite wall time; report actual results\nand any machine or resource constraints rather than making a fragile\ntiming assertion part of the ordinary test suite.\n\n## Implementation Decisions\n\n- Keep the TypeScript package and existing CI gate. The full test command\n  still builds the CLI before tests that execute it, runs the complete\n  non-live suite, and returns a nonzero status on failure.\n- Partition the suite into independent groups that execute in separate\n  Node processes with bounded concurrency. Preserve test discovery and\n  ensure every existing case is included exactly once. A group must not\n  mutate another group's bundle or other shared generated artifacts.\n- Provide readable results for each group, with failures, crashes,\n  incomplete output, and nonzero child exits reliably propagated. Avoid\n  interleaving that makes diagnostics impossible to associate with a\n  group. Preserve the test pipeline's existing failure semantics.\n- Make focused test invocations safe to run concurrently, including\n  independent temporary bundle paths and cleanup. Preserve their existing\n  command-line interface and nonzero failure behavior.\n- Prefer existing dependency injection for sleep and test fakes. Where\n  end-to-end orchestration lacks a suitable seam, add the smallest\n  practical seam at a high boundary. Preserve production retry delays,\n  timeout values, cancellation, and command behavior.\n- Replace avoidable real waits, especially the interrupted inference\n  stream's retry and the doctor timeout, with deterministic control over\n  the relevant delay or signal. Keep representative real-clock tests\n  where they prove integration with actual timers or subprocesses.\n- Investigate the slow gate and Git fixtures with measurements; reduce\n  redundant setup where isolation and behavior allow it. Do not remove a\n  distinct behavioral scenario solely to improve the timing.\n- Keep all tests isolated from user configuration, credentials, and the\n  checkout. Account for process-wide working directories, temporary Git\n  repositories, local HTTP listeners, and cleanup on failure.\n- Use bounded concurrency appropriate to available resources and expose a\n  way to reduce it for constrained or diagnostic environments.\n- Document the commands, worker control, focused-run guarantees, and\n  how to reproduce the timing comparison in contributor documentation.\n\n## Testing Decisions\n\n- A good test verifies observable behavior at the highest practical seam,\n  not private worker scheduling, a specific partition layout, or the\n  implementation of a test double.\n- Exercise the full test command with controlled fixture groups to prove\n  complete execution, isolation, attributable output, and failure\n  propagation for failed assertions, crashes, and incomplete output.\n  Existing test-pipeline command tests provide prior art.\n- Exercise simultaneous focused commands using distinct fixtures, and\n  verify that each reports its own result and exit status. Existing\n  focused-command tests provide prior art.\n- Exercise retry and timeout behavior at existing agent, CLI, and HTTP\n  seams with controlled delays. Verify retry requests, delay decisions,\n  cancellation, and resulting observable outcomes. Existing injected\n  sleep and local inference-server tests provide prior art.\n- Retain representative integration tests using actual Git, gate\n  subprocesses, HTTP, timers, and signals. Preserve assertions about\n  reviewed content, fail-open behavior, and cleanup.\n- Compare repeated full-suite wall times before and after on the same\n  machine and configuration. Report the worker count, test and assertion\n  totals, results, and any variance. Verify the complete CI gate and\n  repeat parallel runs to detect interference; timing is a benchmark,\n  not a hard-coded assertion in the normal test suite.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Changing Roast's production retry, timeout, gate, or review semantics.\n- Deleting meaningful coverage or making live provider tests mandatory.\n- Rewriting the project in another language or replacing the package\n  architecture.\n- Guaranteeing an absolute runtime on every machine or claiming the full\n  integration suite will be instant.\n\n## Further Notes\n\nThe baseline is from an instrumented test-bundle run, not a complete\nunmodified full-suite command. It passed all assertions. Re-establish a\ncomparable uninstrumented baseline before implementing the change.\nLocal HTTP listeners are required for integration tests. The first\nmeasurement attempt could not complete under a sandbox that denied them.\n\n\n---- TICKET ----\n05-control-doctor-timeouts.md\n# 05: Control doctor timeouts in tests\n\n**Blocked by:** 01\n**Touches:** `src/cli/doctor.ts`, `test/cli/doctor.ts`,\nCLI context and test helpers as needed\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n**What to build:** Exercise doctor timeout and cancellation outcomes\nwithout waiting for production-length timeouts, using the smallest useful\ninjection seam while preserving production behavior.\n\n- [ ] A controlled timeout produces the expected observable doctor\n  result without waiting for the production timeout.\n- [ ] Cancellation remains distinguishable and produces the expected\n  observable outcome with resources cleaned up.\n- [ ] Production timeout values remain unchanged and representative\n  real-clock integration coverage remains.\n\n\nThese are records of earlier runs. The ticket or spec may have changed since then; where they disagree, follow the ticket and spec. Do not repeat an approach these notes say failed unless you can see why it failed.\n\n---- PREVIOUS ATTEMPTS AT THIS TICKET ----\n## 2026-11-25 19:21 -- faster-tests/05 attempt 1 -- failed (exit 1)\n\nEffort: medium. Agent exit: 1. Checked items: none.\n\n### Agent notes\n# Attempt notes\n\n- The specified CLI and HTTP seams are used for doctor timeout and cancellation tests. Production deadlines remain unchanged.\n\n- Controlled the first models deadline after the real HTTP request arrives. The CLI reports a timeout and continues to the verifier; focused doctor tests pass. Changed src/cli/doctor.ts and test/cli/doctor.ts.\n\n- Added a real HTTP cancellation test: exit 5, cancellation diagnostic, no partial results or extra requests, and server observes the connection close. Existing behavior passed immediately, so no red test or production fix was needed for this existing guarantee. Focused suite: 241 assertions pass.\n\n- Production deadlines are still 5,000 ms for models and 35,000 ms for roundtrip, verified through the injected deadline factory for both roles. Existing real-clock HTTP request timeout coverage remains in test/llm/client.ts and test/llm/agent-http.ts. The deadline-value test passed immediately because preserving existing behavior requires no implementation change. Focused suite passes 243 assertions; lint and typecheck pass. Full suite is running.\n\n## 2026-11-25 19:22 -- faster-tests/05 attempt 2 -- failed (exit 1)\n\nEffort: high. Agent exit: 1. Checked items: none.\n\nThe agent left no notes.\n\n## 2026-11-25 19:23 -- faster-tests/05 attempt 3 -- failed (exit 1)\n\nEffort: high. Agent exit: 1. Checked items: none.\n\nThe agent left no notes.\n\n## 2026-11-25 19:57 -- faster-tests/05 attempt 4 -- failed (tests)\n\nEffort: high. Agent exit: 0. Checked items: none.\n\nTest gate failed.\nLast 40 lines of `05-control-doctor-timeouts.attempt4.test.log`:\n```\n    roast: verifying 2 finding(s) with verifier-model (profile=vfake protocol=chat)\n    roast: run 20261126T035658Z-692b5293 · report /private/var/folders/wc/j7p9ktnx3d99v5xm95s9h2480000gn/T/roast-review-os9TK7/work/.roast/runs/20261126T035658Z-692b5293/report.md\n    ✔ one verifier conversation\n    ✔ should be equal\n    ✔ first decided\n    ✔ second undecided\n    ✔ should be equal\n\n  aborting during verification still writes the report\n\n    ✔ roast: no pre-commit gate in this repo; run `roast gate enable` to install it (non-interactive runs never install Git hooks without consent)\n    roast: using base 'master'\n    roast: finder=finder-model profile=fake protocol=chat endpoint=http://127.0.0.1:62783/v1\n    roast: verifying 1 finding(s) with verifier-model (profile=vfake protocol=chat)\n    roast: run 20261126T035658Z-25b70ebe · report /private/var/folders/wc/j7p9ktnx3d99v5xm95s9h2480000gn/T/roast-review-pfeSIs/work/.roast/runs/20261126T035658Z-25b70ebe/report.md\n    ✔ should be equal\n    ✔ report.md\n    ✔ should be equal\n    ✔ should be equal\n\n\n\n  Failed Tests: There were 2 failures\n\n    aborting build during linguist check-attr rejects with AbortError\n\n      ✖ timed out waiting for /private/var/folders/wc/j7p9ktnx3d99v5xm95s9h2480000gn/T/roast-wrapgit-BGATrO/pid\n\n\n    aborting build during rename compaction rejects with AbortError\n\n      ✖ timed out waiting for /private/var/folders/wc/j7p9ktnx3d99v5xm95s9h2480000gn/T/roast-wrapgit-UZyIOQ/pid\n\n\n  total:     7699\n  passing:   7697\n  failing:   2\n  duration:  4m 31.4s\n\n\n```\n\n### Agent notes\n# Attempt notes\n\n- Continued from commits f99546e and 601569c. The control